      "raw_answer": "{\n  \"sections\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"set-user-role\",\n      \"title\": \"New admin-only endpoint to change a user's role, with self-promotion guard\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The single added hunk introduces PUT /users/<id>/role. It is one cohesive access-control concern: it enforces the admin role via @require_role(\\\"admin\\\"), blocks an admin from changing their own role (g.current_user.id == user_id), and validates the new role against a hard-coded allowlist (user/manager/admin) before persisting it to User.role. All of these checks implement the same policy rule (security-policy.md \u00a72: 'Changing a user's role requires the admin role. A user must NEVER be able to change their own role or grant themselves additional privileges'), so they belong in one review section. The grouping depends on the require_role decorator (which sets g.current_user and enforces ROLE_RANK) and the User.role column that the endpoint mutates.\",\n      \"hunks\": [\"app/routes/users.py#0\"],\n      \"context\": [\n        {\"path\": \"app/auth.py\", \"symbol\": \"require_role\", \"start_line\": 69, \"end_line\": 85, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Decorator applied to set_user_role; enforces ROLE_RANK >= admin and sets g.current_user used by the self-promotion check.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/auth.py\", \"symbol\": \"ROLE_RANK\", \"start_line\": 21, \"end_line\": 21, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Defines the user<manager<admin ranking that require_role uses to gate the endpoint.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/models.py\", \"symbol\": \"User\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 40, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"The User.role column (line 30) is the field the endpoint mutates; to_dict (line 36) is used in the response.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/routes/users.py\", \"symbol\": \"update_user\", \"start_line\": 41, \"end_line\": 55, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Adjacent profile-update endpoint; confirms the new role endpoint is a distinct, separate authorization path (role change is admin-only, not owner-or-admin).\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
