      "raw_answer": "Based on my review, the new `set_user_role` endpoint correctly enforces the policy: it uses the mandated `@require_role(\"admin\")` decorator (auth.py:69-85, which authenticates and gates on ROLE_RANK >= admin), and it blocks self-promotion via `g.current_user.id == user_id` (users.py:60-61). The role value is validated against a hard-coded allowlist (users.py:64). This matches security-policy.md \u00a72 (\"Changing a user's role requires the admin role. A user must NEVER be able to change their own role\") and api-spec.md (`/users/<id>/role` PUT: admin only; self-promotion forbidden). No authorization flaw is introduced by this section.\n\n{\n  \"findings\": []\n}",
